in Minoan and Mycenaean art. Observations draw upon historical scholarship and 
recent discoveries to question and affirm previous conclusions related to the 
ring's motifs and their implications. [...] The many years of research that led
to the present paper on the so-called Ring of Nestor (CMS VI, nο. 277), with 
the documentation of its authenticity, have offered me the opportunity to 
discuss the cases of erroneous identifications of some Creto-Mycenaean gold 
